Team,

Following up on the security audit, here is the refactoring plan:

Phase 1 (this sprint):
- Refactor hash_password to use argon2 instead of SHA256
- Update verify_password to support both old and new hash formats
  during the migration period
- Move JWT secret to environment config

Phase 2 (next sprint):
- Redesign generate_jwt_token to support refresh token rotation
- Add rate limiting to the login function in auth_routes
- Update register to enforce stronger password requirements

The create_user function in database.py will need a migration to
store the new hash format. The User model in models.py should add
a hash_version field.

Note: The require_admin decorator needs to be audited separately
since it chains through require_auth and verify_jwt_token.

Let me know if you have questions.
